The most recent Mercedes-Benz C Class with the 'Avantgarde' trim is the W206 generation, launched around 2021. The 'Avantgarde' trim is a core offering on this model in many markets. I will base the evaluation on the W206 C200 Avantgarde sedan, as it's a common powertrain for this trim.

Based on the search results, here are some specifications for the W206 C200 Avantgarde sedan:
- Engine: 1.5L 4-cylinder Turbo Petrol with 48V Mild Hybrid (EQ Boost)
- HP: 204 PS (201 hp) + 20 hp from EQ Boost
- Torque: 300 Nm (221 lb-ft) + 200 Nm from EQ Boost
- Transmission: 9G-Tronic 9-speed automatic
- Drive Type: Rear-Wheel Drive (4MATIC AWD available on some engines/markets)
- 0-60 mph: ~7.1 seconds (0-100 km/h in 7.3 seconds)
- Top Speed: 246 km/h (~153 mph)
- Length: 4751 mm (187.0 inches)
- Width: 1820 mm (71.7 inches) (excluding mirrors)
- Height: 1437 mm (56.6 inches)
- Wheelbase: 2865 mm (112.8 inches)
- Ground Clearance: 9.7 cm (~3.8 inches)
- Cargo Space: 455 liters (~16.1 cu ft)
- Seats: 5
- Price New (UK/Europe): Starts around £38,785 / €41,138 (C180/C200) (Equivalent to ~$45,000 - $50,000+ USD depending on market/options)
- Insurance Group (UK): 33-45 (range for W206 C-Class)
- MPG (Combined WLTP): ~37-44 mpg (6.4 L/100km)
- CO2 (WLTP): ~146-154 g/km
- Electrification: Mild Hybrid (48V system with Integrated Starter Generator)
- Electric Range: Very limited (mild hybrid boost only)
- Charge Speed: Not applicable (mild hybrid)
- Interior: 11.9-inch central touchscreen, 12.3-inch digital instrument cluster, MBUX infotainment, wireless CarPlay/Android Auto, heated memory seats, dual-zone climate, ambient lighting, panoramic sunroof (optional/higher trims)
- ADAS: Basic ADAS standard (Active Brake Assist), more advanced features optional (Adaptive Cruise Control, Lane Keeping Assist, Blind Spot Assist, 360 camera, Parking Assist)
- Headlights: LED High Performance standard, DIGITAL LIGHT optional
- USB Ports: Six 100W fast charging USB ports mentioned for some trims

